{:id :EACL-FORMAL-011
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "recursive-shadow/reverse-self-permission/resource-counters"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :other
 :affected-versions ["PR 101 worktree before dimensional shadow comparison"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike :third-party]
 :root-cause
 "The host reverse evaluator installed self-permission consumers immediately, while the generated indexed engine represented the same authorization-affecting registration as explicit FIFO work. Values happened to agree, but cumulative enqueues and maximum queue depth differed by one and the two transition systems could not support a dimensionally exact resource refinement."
 :fix
 "The host reverse evaluator now queues consumer registration before the dependent goal, matching the generated transition system. Shadow mode independently captures cache-free host and generated counters plus retained logical units and compares them without disclosing authorization values."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.formal.state-trace-differential-test/recursive-shadow-compares-complete-public-results"
  "eacl.backend.v8-test reverse traversal characterization"
